---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import {catalogue} from '../data/content.mjs';
const b=import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/,'');
const l=(p)=>`${b}/${p}/`;
---
<Site>
  <section class="hero home-hero">
    <picture><source media="(max-width: 640px)" srcset={`${b}/media/heroes/meeting-mobile.webp`}/><img class="hero-image" src={`${b}/media/heroes/meeting.webp`} alt="An imagined luminous archive opening towards a sunlit Australian coast" width="2400" height="1350" fetchpriority="high"/></picture>
    <div class="hero-shade"></div>
    <div class="hero-copy"><p class="intro-name">Luke Nathan Hayes</p><h1>A curious meeting<br/>of <em>worlds.</em></h1><p class="hero-deck">An invitation to explore my work, the synchronicities, and the possibilities of Joyful Responsible Abundance.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button light" href={l('start')}>Come and explore <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={l('why-this-interview')}>The conversation that sparked this</a></div></div>
    <div class="hero-bottom"><span>11 September 2026 · 11:11 am · Australia</span><span>Concept artwork · an imagined meeting place</span></div>
  </section>
  <section class="section opening"><div><p class="section-number">01 / A beginning</p><h2>Tim, if our paths<br/>meet here, <em>welcome.</em></h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Your interview sent me back through years of ideas, documents and projects. I recognised threads I have been following in my own way: consciousness, materials, memory, meaning and the futures we might help bring into being.</p><p>I wrote through your website at 11:11 am Australian time. Five minutes later, after laughing about the synchronicity with friends, I wrote again to share that moment with you or your secretary. Two messages, one joyful opening.</p><a class="text-link dark-link" href={l('11-11')}>The story of 11:11 ↗</a></div></section>
  <section class="section doorways"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Follow the thread<br/>that <em>calls to you.</em></h2><p>There is no prescribed order. Begin with a conversation, an idea, a source or a world you would like to imagine.</p></div><div class="doorway-grid">{[
    ['The interview','The questions and moments that caught my imagination.','interview','conversation'],
    ['My work & its connections','Aura, Queens Venture, sovereign networks and the long game.','network','network'],
    ['An open research horizon','Arks, materials, resonance and the pleasure of asking better questions.','research','matter']
  ].map(([title,desc,path,img])=><a class="doorway" href={l(path)}><img src={`${b}/media/heroes/${img}.webp`} width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" alt=""/><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{desc}</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div></a>)}</div></section>
  <section class="feature-split"><img src={`${b}/media/heroes/meeting.webp`} width="1672" height="941" loading="lazy" alt="An imagined archive opening towards a luminous coast"/><div><p class="section-number">02 / A thread through time</p><h2>One Aura.<br/><em>Many doorways.</em></h2><p>From handwritten reflections and pre-AI presentations to today's AI-assisted explorations, I keep returning to a question: how might we understand ourselves, care for one another and grow something worth sharing?</p><p>The collection here is a window into that journey. Hundreds more documents, presentations and personal handwritten journals sit beyond it.</p><a class="button" href={l('timeline')}>Explore the unfolding story ↗</a></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Keep the originals<br/><em>close to the story.</em></h2><p>Read the interview. Turn through the slides. Wander into the repositories. Follow a connection and see what it opens.</p></div><div class="archive-links"><a href={l('library')}><strong>{catalogue.sources.length}</strong><span>documents and images<br/>in the reading collection</span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a><a href={l('gallery')}><strong>97</strong><span>slides across<br/>six original presentations</span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a><a href={l('projects')}><strong>152</strong><span>projects in the supplied<br/>Project Atlas snapshot</span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a></div></section>
  <section class="closing-note"><p>Bold in imagination.<br/>Humble in exploration.<br/><em>Joyful in the possibilities.</em></p><a href={l('culture')}>Joyful Responsible Abundance ↗</a></section>
</Site>
